  "helpTitle": "How to play",
  "helpBody": "A four-digit plate number appears. Keep the digits in their order and insert operators around them so that the equation becomes true. Digits with nothing between them form a single number (4 and 1 make 41).\n\nEvery “_” mark is a place where symbols can go: before, between and after the digits, and on both sides of the = sign. Tap a “_” to select it, then tap operators to insert them there. Whenever another symbol still fits after the ones you placed, a new “_” shows up, so you can chain symbols such as √( or )!; impossible combinations such as ++ are refused. To type a symbol between two others, tap one of them (or use the arrow keys): the cursor moves next to it and the new symbol goes exactly there. The backspace key removes the symbol right before the cursor. The = sign is always on the plate: to move it, drag it to another “_”, or tap it and then tap a “_”, or select a “_” and press the = key.\n\nTap Check to validate your answer. Correct answers score points (Easy 1, Intermediate 2, Advanced 3, Hard 4) and that number never shows up again at that level. Only plates that have a solution are dealt. Stuck? Skip the number.",
  "helpExample": "Example with 8131:",
  "helpOperators": "Operators per level",
  "close": "Close",

