  "tourDone": "Start playing",
  "tourReplay": "Show the tour",
  "tourDisplayTitle": "The display",
  "tourDisplayBody": "The four digits of the plate are here, in the order you must keep. Above them are the level and your score. The bottom line tells you how much each side of the equation is worth, or what is wrong with it.",
  "tourMarksTitle": "Where symbols go",
  "tourMarksBody": "Each “_” is a place for symbols. Tap one to select it (it blinks), then tap operators. When another symbol still fits, a new “_” appears beside it. To type between two symbols, tap one of them.",
  "tourEqualsTitle": "The = sign",
  "tourEqualsBody": "It splits the plate into the two sides of the equation. To change where the plate is split, drag it to another “_”, or tap it and then tap a “_”.",
  "tourFormulaTitle": "Rendered formula",
  "tourFormulaBody": "As you type, your equation is drawn here in mathematical notation, with roots, fractions and exponents, so you can check that it means what you intended.",
  "tourLevelTitle": "Level",
  "tourLevelBody": "Tap or slide to choose a level. Harder levels have fewer operators and are worth more points: Easy 1, Intermediate 2, Advanced 3, Hard 4.",
  "tourOperatorsTitle": "Operators",
  "tourOperatorsBody": "Tap an operator to insert it where the cursor is. The keys change with the level. Rest the pointer on a key, or long-press it, to see its name.",
  "tourEditTitle": "Moving and erasing",
  "tourEditBody": "The arrows move the cursor through every place a symbol can go. The backspace key removes the symbol before the cursor, and Clear removes them all.",
  "tourSkipTitle": "Skip number",
  "tourSkipBody": "Stuck? Skip to another plate. Every plate you get has at least one solution.",
  "tourVerifyTitle": "Check",
  "tourVerifyBody": "When both sides are equal, tap Check. A right answer scores and brings a new plate. A wrong one shows why and leaves your symbols in place, so you can keep trying.",
  "tourMenuTitle": "Menu",
  "tourMenuBody": "Play, the plates you have solved, help (where you can see this tour again) and settings: theme, colors, font, language and sound."
